Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 08:58:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Table grid snapped to the scan (port of snap_table.py)

- app/services/table_snap.py: vertical rules (open >= 100 px, <= 12 px
  thick) and horizontal rules (>= 150 px) whose both ends touch a vertical
  rule, so Devanagari headlines are rejected; positions clustered at 10 px.
  Cells from the table HTML (th/td, colspan, rowspan, <br>, literal \n),
  boxes from the grid, empty cells kept, header_rows from leading <th> rows,
  one table line per printed line in each cell, ruling_lines from the
  detected segments (partial stays partial). A rows/cols mismatch leaves the
  table unchanged with a warning. Fixes over the script: cell text is
  HTML-escaped, a row fully covered by rowspans no longer counts as a
  header row, handwritten flags kept, ruling_style full/partial measured.
- POST /documents/{id}/snap-table {doc?, element_id?, html?}
  -> {record, warnings, info}
- 'Fit cells to image' becomes 'Fit cells to scan' and uses the snap
- opencv-python-headless added to backend dependencies

